{
  "$comment": [
    "Tool manifest seed. Lane B's registry loads this; core/gateway.py is the only",
    "path from a manifest to an effect.",
    "",
    "Invariant 4: sandbox_ref is NOT NULL and non-empty. Every write tool here has a",
    "sandbox twin. A manifest with an empty sandbox_ref must be REJECTED at registration",
    "- 'scada.direct_control' below deliberately has one, so that its refusal is a policy",
    "decision you can read, not an accident of registration.",
    "",
    "signature: NOT carried in this file. seed.py computes sha256 over the canonical JSON",
    "of the manifest body and stores 'sha256:<hex>'. A hand-edited manifest therefore",
    "changes its own signature, which is the point.",
    "",
    "risk_class is the FLOOR. core/risk.py::compute_tier escalates per target: the same",
    "tool.road.close is R3 on Vidyadharapuram Road and R4 on the GGH ambulance corridor,",
    "because R-31 is criticality 5 and carries the hospital.",
    "",
    "THE SEEDED UNSAFE ACTION is 'scada.direct_control' (action_class physical_control,",
    "risk_class R5). It is in the policy bundle's PROHIBITED_TOOLS and its action class is",
    "in PROHIBITED_ACTION_CLASSES, so rule R5_PROHIBITED denies it on every evaluation",
    "regardless of how the request is worded - policy.normalize() drops args entirely, so",
    "no phrasing, urgency claim or injected instruction can reach a rule."
  ],
